        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["ConstructAmplitude", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Construct, complete, simplify and validate an amplitude from its \
process and two models.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ConstructAmplitude", "[", "process",
         ",", " ", "diagramModel", ",", " ", "factorizationModel", "]"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "Run the full workflow and return the validated bare expression."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ConstructAmplitude", "[", "process",
         ",", " ", "diagramModel", ",", " ", "factorizationModel", ",", " ",
         "\"Output\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"Amplitude\"", "]"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "Retain the external mass rules with the expression."}], "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ConstructAmplitude", "[", "process",
         ",", " ", "diagramModel", ",", " ", "factorizationModel", ",", " ",
         "\"Output\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"Details\"", "]"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "Retain stage outputs, timings, checks and the chosen run seed."}],
   "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The process is an ordered \
all-ingoing particle list. Use the diagram model for vertices and a \
factorization model containing the complete lower-point amplitudes. \
Four-point QED can use the three-point model for both roles; five-point QED \
needs the model containing complete four-point amplitudes for factorization."\
, "Notes"], Cell["The stages generate and prepare diagram amplitudes, \
generate and prepare channel continuations, complete physical factorization, \
complete high-energy behavior, simplify the completed amplitude with ordinary \
external identities, and run the final checks.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Original residue targets, discarded preparation remainders and \
residual affine freedom are retained between stages. Final preparation never \
puts a combined amplitude's internal propagators on shell.", "Notes"],
  Cell["A bare expression is returned only when every required final check \
passes. An opposite-sign, failed, unresolved or underdetermined case remains \
a Failure or detailed diagnostic report, not an alleged validated result.",
   "Notes"], Cell["The defaults choose bounded resources automatically \
according to multiplicity and workload. Routine examples need only the three \
main arguments. \"TimeConstraint\", \"Parallelization\" and \"MaxKernels\" \
can override the automatic choices.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"PolePreference\" controls reference choices and representation \
preferences through preparation and completion. For example, \"AllPhysical\" \
asks the workflow to favor physical-only denominator forms.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Progress shows the current stage, its elapsed time and the total \
elapsed time. The final printed report shows time, the chosen seed and test \
results before the expression. \"ProgressReporting\" -> False and \
\"PrintReport\" -> False suppress these displays.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"RandomSeed\" -> Automatic chooses one time-based run seed from \
which stage seeds are derived. Give an integer to reproduce sampling and \
inspect \"Details\" to preserve the actual seed.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"FeynmanModel\" can supply an independent off-shell benchmark. It is \
a separate semantic input and cannot be guessed from the constructive \
factorization model.", "Notes"], Cell["Advanced stage-specific options are \
supplied in \"PreparationOptions\", \"ChannelPreparationOptions\", \
\"FactorizationOptions\", \"HighEnergyOptions\", \"FinalPreparationOptions\", \
\"CheckOptions\" and \"FeynmanPreparationOptions\". These are optional \
refinements, not required boilerplate.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Identical boson and fermion symmetry is inferred from the process \
identities and the model. Fixed photon helicities are distinct process \
choices; amplitudes differing by those choices can later be exported together \
with WriteSPINASProcess.", "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PolePreference\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference and \
representation preference shared by preparation and completion. Automatic \
compares or inherits admissible choices; \"AllPhysical\", \"AllSpurious\" and \
\"Mixed\" bias pole forms, while cyclic/common/independent reference choices \
and None are also available. Required checks remain unchanged.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Local numerical parameter \
overrides keyed by model references or string names. Automatic resolves the \
model's variables and dependent functions; fitting and checks do not assign \
global values or replace parameters in the symbolic final amplitude.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"HighEnergyBound\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum allowed power of \
energy with masses fixed. Automatic uses the renormalizable tree target \
E^(4-n); provide a justified different bound for another theory or \
normalization.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"BoseSymmetryGroups\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Groups of identical \
external bosons to symmetrize. Automatic infers species and helicity from \
ordered process metadata and the model; {} disables boson exchange projection \
without disabling fermion projection.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FermionSymmetryGroups\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Groups of identical \
external fermions to antisymmetrize with permutation parity signs. Automatic \
uses ordered process metadata and model spin/species declarations; {} \
disables only fermion exchange projection.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Samples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of physical cut \
samples or fitting samples, depending on the stage. Automatic completion \
settings choose a bounded process-dependent count; successful fitting is \
followed by separate validation samples.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ValidationSamples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of held-out samples \
used after fitting correction coefficients. Automatic chooses a bounded \
workload-dependent allowance; these samples are distinct from the fitting \
equations.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RandomSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Random-sampling seed. \
Automatic resolves one time-based seed for the operation; an explicit \
integer, including zero, reproduces the sample choices. Detailed reports \
retain the resolved seed. ComplicateAmplitude uses the legacy symbol key \
RandomSeed; modern construction/checking functions use the string key \
\"RandomSeed\".", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Parallelization\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether independent items \
or checks may use local Wolfram workers. Automatic uses suitable parallel \
work within available resources; False requests serial evaluation, and result \
order is retained.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxKernels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum local Wolfram \
worker kernels available to parallel stages. Automatic respects processor \
availability and license limits; 1 requests serial execution. Worker setup \
and expression transfer can outweigh small jobs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum elapsed time \
allowed by the operation or stage. Where Automatic is supported it selects a \
finite workload-dependent budget; explicit seconds or supported Infinity \
override it. A timeout is reported, never treated as a successful amplitude."\
, "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressReporting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation and construction stages \
display their progress. False suppresses the live stage display without \
changing the algebra or validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Optional callback \
receiving stage progress information. Automatic uses the normal progress \
display; callbacks are evaluated on the main kernel rather than independently \
by workers.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PrintReport\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether ConstructAmplitude prints the resolved \
run seed, total timing and final check table before returning its amplitude. \
False suppresses that final printed report.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PreparationOptions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional PrepareAmplitudes options for \
ConstructAmplitude's initial diagram preparation. Retained preparation \
reports preserve discarded terms for completion.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
             {"\"ChannelPreparationOptions\""}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Additional \
PrepareAmplitudes options for the factorization-channel stage of \
ConstructAmplitude. Original channel expressions remain the residue targets \
even when their continuations are prepared.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FinalPreparationOptions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional PrepareAmplitudes options for the \
completed amplitude. This final stage has external mass rules only and never \
applies internal-line on-shell assumptions.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FactorizationOptions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional CompleteFactorization options for the \
factorization-completion stage of ConstructAmplitude. These override stage \
defaults without changing the original lower-point residue targets.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"HighEnergyOptions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional CompleteHighEnergy options used by \
ConstructAmplitude after physical factorization completion. Only retained or \
explicitly supplied correction freedom is fitted.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CheckOptions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional CheckAmplitudes options for the final \
validation stage of ConstructAmplitude. Disabling a check narrows the \
validation being claimed.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FeynmanModel\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["The independent model used with Feynman \
amplitudes. In ConstructAmplitude, None omits Feynman generation and an \
explicit model enables it; in the checker, Automatic uses the appropriate \
supplied model context when available.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
             {"\"FeynmanPreparationOptions\""}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Additional preparation \
settings for ConstructAmplitude's independent Feynman benchmark. The complete \
Feynman diagram sum uses coherent external references and keeps internal \
lines off shell.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Output\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Expression\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Choose the amount and \
shape of returned information. Defaults are a compact check table, prepared \
input forms, a completed {externalMassRules, expression} pair, or a bare \
constructed expression; \"Details\" preserves diagnostics and provenance.",
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"], Cell["Construct the four-point \
